{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 11 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.math.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final BigInteger MOD = BigInteger.valueOf(998244353L);\n    static final long MODL = 998244353L;\n    static final long INV2 = 499122177L;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(br);\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        long n = sc.nextInt();\n        long m = sc.nextInt();\n        long l = sc.nextInt();\n        long r = sc.nextInt();\n        long cells = n * m;\n        String ans = solve(l, r, cells);\n        if (cells % 2 == 1) {\n            out.print(ans);\n        } else {\n            out.println(ans);\n        }\n        out.flush();\n        sc.close();\n        br.close();\n    }\n\n    static String solve(long l, long r, long cells) {\n        long k = r - l;\n        long even = k / 2 + 1;\n        long odd = (k + 1) / 2;\n        if (cells % 2 == 1) {\n            return BigInteger.valueOf(k + 1).modPow(BigInteger.valueOf(cells), MOD).toString();\n        }\n        BigInteger temp1 = BigInteger.valueOf(even + odd).modPow(BigInteger.valueOf(cells), MOD);\n        BigInteger temp2 = BigInteger.valueOf(even - odd).modPow(BigInteger.valueOf(cells), MOD);\n        long sum = (temp1.longValue() + temp2.longValue()) % MODL;\n        long ans = sum * INV2 % MODL;\n        return String.valueOf(ans);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <cstdint>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 998244353LL;\nconst long long INV2 = 499122177LL;\n\nlong long modpow(long long a, long long b, long long mod) {\n    long long res = 1;\n    a %= mod;\n    while (b) {\n        if (b & 1) res = (res * a) % mod;\n        a = (a * a) % mod;\n        b >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nstring solve(long long l, long long r, long long cells) {\n    long long k = r - l;\n    long long even = k / 2 + 1;\n    long long odd = (k + 1) / 2;\n    if (cells % 2 == 1) {\n        long long base = k + 1;\n        long long ans = modpow(base, cells, MOD);\n        return to_string(ans);\n    } else {\n        long long temp1 = modpow(even + odd, cells, MOD);\n        long long temp2 = modpow(even - odd, cells, MOD);\n        long long sum = (temp1 + temp2) % MOD;\n        long long ans = (sum * INV2) % MOD;\n        return to_string(ans);\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n, m, l, r;\n    cin >> n >> m >> l >> r;\n    long long cells = n * m;\n    string ans = solve(l, r, cells);\n    if (cells % 2 == 1) {\n        cout << ans << flush;\n    } else {\n        cout << ans << endl;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.99\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -5.94836674281396e-05, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.009163584560155869, -1.0132738680113107e-